    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d493-a1">

                <pb facs="0812" n="678" xml:id="pg678"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sewall to Mr.
                            Becker.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate-General of the United States of America, Apia,
                                Samoa</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Apia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-01-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 31, 1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your communication of 18th
                    January, I have to state that while the position of Her Britannic Majesty’s
                    vice-consul, Mr. Wilson, renders the negotiations proposed hy you impossible,
                    yet that in my opinion it is advisable that some understanding be reached by
                    ourselves respecting the pilot station, the house of which is occupied by a
                    German subject and the land owned by a citizen of the United States. I should be
                    glad to have your opinion about this matter.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harold Marsh
                                Sewall</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Consul
                            General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
